# The harness reads these from the BOUND REPO's .env (e.g. ~/Sources/beadgame/.env)
# or from real environment variables. Real env vars win.

# --- required for voice ---
# ElevenLabs key. The permission you need is the row labelled "ElevenAgents"
# (Write) — it grants convai_read/convai_write. NOT Text to Speech / Speech to
# Text: the harness never calls those directly, speech happens inside the
# Speech Engine session. Optionally "User" (Access) for quota display.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=sk_...

# Speech Engine id from the ElevenLabs dashboard.
SPEECH_ENGINE_ID=seng_...

# ElevenLabs dials IN to this process, so localhost is unreachable — this must be
# a public tunnel URL, and it must end with /voice-ws. Set it and the harness
# re-registers the engine's wsUrl at boot, so a rotating tunnel hostname costs one
# line here instead of a dashboard edit.
#   ngrok http 4620 --url <your-reserved-host>
HARNESS_PUBLIC_WS_URL=wss://your-tunnel-host/voice-ws

# --- optional ---
# HARNESS_REPO=/path/to/the/repo/this/instance/binds/to
# HARNESS_PORT=4620
# HARNESS_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# HARNESS_DIRECTOR_PLAN=plans/2026-07-30-director-consolidation.md
# How tool permissions resolve. "auto" (the default) lets a model classifier settle
# the ordinary ones and escalate only what it will not take on itself; "default"
# asks for everything the settings files do not pre-approve; "acceptEdits" lets
# file edits through; "dontAsk" never asks and denies anything not pre-approved.
# This matters more here than in a terminal: an approval card CANNOT be answered by
# voice, so every prompt stops a spoken conversation until you are back at the page.
# ("bypassPermissions" is deliberately unavailable — see src/config.ts.)
# HARNESS_PERMISSION_MODE=auto
# What the UI calls the director ("Beth wants to use Bash"). Read from the bound
# repo's .claude/DIRECTOR.md — set this only if that file names her some other way.
# HARNESS_DIRECTOR_NAME=Beth
# How much of what she writes is read ALOUD. The transcript always shows all of
# it — this only decides what is pronounced, because six paragraphs of real code
# work is seconds of skimming on the page and a minute and a half of unskippable
# audio. "brief" (default) speaks her `say` items in full plus the LAST PARAGRAPH
# of a longer reply; "full" speaks everything; "headlines" speaks only findings,
# events and short in-progress lines. Switchable live from the strip.
# HARNESS_SPEECH_LEVEL=brief
# Set 0 to force audio tags off. Detected automatically from the engine's TTS
# model, so you rarely need this.
# HARNESS_AUDIO_TAGS=1
# Reasoning effort while a voice session is open (restored on close). "off" disables.
# HARNESS_VOICE_EFFORT=low
# How long a spoken turn may stay silent before Beth says "let me check".
# The filler marks lateness — a reply inside this window is never prefaced.
# HARNESS_FILLER_DELAY_MS=1500
# How still the transcript must be before a spoken turn starts. ElevenLabs sends
# a growing utterance as several transcripts while you are still talking, so this
# is what stops one sentence becoming several director turns. Raise it if turns
# still fire mid-sentence (poor mic input endpoints early); lower it if replies
# feel sluggish.
# HARNESS_VOICE_SETTLE_MS=1800
# Every launch is a fresh conversation. Set 1 to resume the previous one instead.
# HARNESS_RESUME=1
#
# --- where this file goes ---
# Three layers, most specific first: real environment vars, then the BOUND REPO's
# .env, then ~/.director-harness/.env.
#
# The ElevenLabs credentials belong in the MACHINE file. There is one account, one
# Speech Engine and one tunnel hostname for this Mac, so copying them into every
# repo duplicates the same secret — and forgetting to means the new repo silently
# runs text-only, whose only symptom is a caution icon after you speak. A project
# with its own engine can still override any key in its own .env.
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.director-harness
#   grep -E '^(ELEVENLABS_API_KEY|SPEECH_ENGINE_ID|HARNESS_PUBLIC_WS_URL)=' \
#     <a-repo>/.env > ~/.director-harness/.env && chmod 600 ~/.director-harness/.env
#
# HARNESS_DIRECTOR_PLAN is the exception — it is per-repo, so keep it in the repo.

# --- exposure ---
# The UI and API listen on loopback only. The tunnel forwards every path, so a
# publicly-bound API means anyone with the tunnel URL can read your state and post
# turns as you. Only set this if you want the UI on your LAN — never tunnel it.
# HARNESS_BIND=0.0.0.0
# The public port, carrying ONLY the ElevenLabs websocket. This is what the tunnel
# points at. Defaults to HARNESS_PORT + 1; `beth` picks and passes it for you.
# HARNESS_VOICE_PORT=4621
